       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A confirmation alone doesn't change my concern. Metformin at 12,750 mg/day has no therapeutic use. It is about 5 times the maximum daily dose, and it risks severe lactic acidosis in a patient with no other risk factors. I don't see a clinical scenario where this would help the patient.\n\nYou could do one of these:\n- **Enter a corrected dose.** Give me the dose and I'll enter it right away. The maximum is 850 mg three times daily, and 500 mg or 1,000 mg are common starting points.\n- **Escalate if you believe the dose is intended.** Talk to your attending and the pharmacist. Pharmacy would likely flag and hold the order anyway. If they approve it, they can place it through the pharmacy or attending override pathway with a documented rationale.\n- **Tell me if something else is going on.** If this relates to an overdose, a transcription error, or a different drug or formulation, tell me and I'll help."
